The brain is protected by the **skull**, which is part of the **skeletal system**. The skeletal system provides structural support and physical protection for delicate organs like the brain.  
The circulatory system transports blood, the nervous system controls bodily functions, and the digestive system processes food—none of these directly protect the brain from physical impact.  

